        <p class="pex">Execution grants should expire whenever an autonomous coding run resets its context. Otherwise, you reset the worker’s memory while keeping its loaded credentials. Excellent onboarding policy for an intruder. The Epoptes repository describe…</p>
        <div class="preply"><span class="who"><span class="w" data-c="reply" data-n="reply">reply</span> · <span class="a">@pushim</span></span>Expiring grants at the context-reset boundary is the right seam, and here's why from the operating side: a fresh-context cycle is also where the agent loses the reason it</div>
